From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:46:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Touch ID hint

With TouchIdHint = true, while /run/tiny-dfr/touchid says "waiting" (a
helper watching fprintd: sudo, the lock screen) the bar right of Esc shows
TouchIdIcon and TouchIdText with an arrow to the sensor, the key right of
the Touch Bar, as on macOS. "retry" shows TouchIdRetryText (orange), a
match flashes a green tick and "nomatch" TouchIdFailText (red) for 0.9 s,
even when "idle" follows at once. A "waiting" older than 60 s is taken as
stale. With Animations the arrow moves towards the sensor, 15 frames a
second of only its own area. Only Esc stays usable under the hint. The
file is "<state> <ms since the epoch>" and is watched with inotify; the
PNG preview shows the four states.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
